= Solution
{parent=a}

Substituting the line into the <hyperbola> gives
$$
7x^2-(x+1)^2=7
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
3x^2-x-4=(3x-4)(x+1)=0.
$$
The two <polynomial roots> give all intersections:
$$
\boxed{(x,y)=(-1,0),\qquad (4/3,7/3).}
$$
Both satisfy the original line as well as the curve.

= b
{parent=5}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Put the equation into standard <ellipse> form:
$$
\frac{(x-1)^2}{3}+\frac{y^2}{3/2}=1.
$$
The <centre> is $(1,0)$, with horizontal semiaxis $\sqrt3$ and vertical semiaxis $\sqrt{3/2}$. Its four axis vertices are $(1\pm\sqrt3,0)$ and $(1,\pm\sqrt{3/2})$; the <ellipse> meets the vertical coordinate axis at $(0,\pm1)$.

\Image[paper-1-ellipse.png]
{title=The displaced ellipse with its centre, semiaxes and coordinate-axis intersections}

