The original line meets the horizontal axis at $(-3/2,0)$. A perpendicular line has slope $-1/2$, the negative reciprocal of $2$, so
$$
\boxed{y=-\frac12\left(x+\frac32\right)
=-\frac x2-\frac34.}
$$
Substituting $x=-3/2$ verifies the required common point.

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

For the <partial fraction decomposition>, write $A/(x-4)+B/(x+9)$. Clearing denominators gives $13(x+1)=A(x+9)+B(x-4)$. Substitution at $x=4$ and $x=-9$ yields $A=5$ and $B=8$, hence
$$
\boxed{\frac{13(x+1)}{(x-4)(x+9)}=\frac5{x-4}+\frac8{x+9},\qquad x\ne4,-9.}
$$

= 11
{parent=Paper 1}
